# CVE-2026-33845 — GnuTLS: DoS via DTLS zero-length fragment (libgnutls30t64)
# Severity  : CRITICAL
# Status    : no fixed version available (affected, 2026-05-06)
# Rationale : Parrot serves HTTP over TCP only — DTLS (UDP-based TLS) is never
#             used, so this vulnerability is not reachable in our runtime.
#             Re-evaluate when a patched version lands in debian:13.
CVE-2026-33845

# CVE-2026-7598 — libssh2: integer overflow via large username/password (libssh2-1t64)
# Severity  : CRITICAL
# Status    : no fixed version available (affected, 2026-05-11)
# Rationale : libssh2 is a transitive Debian system dependency; Parrot does not
#             initiate or accept SSH connections — the vulnerable SSH handshake
#             code path is never executed. Re-evaluate when a patched version
#             lands in debian:13.
CVE-2026-7598
